# Two paths decide what CI checks, and a pull request can change them along
# with the work under review:
#
#   /blueprint/roadmap/README.md  its open_statements setting decides whether
#                                 a theorem may merge with a sorry proof
#   /.github/                     the workflows, the audit script, and this file
#
# To use the rules, replace @OWNER with GitHub users, or visible teams, that
# have write access to the repository, and uncomment them. GitHub then asks
# those owners to review pull requests that change these paths. A merge waits
# for their approval only once a branch protection rule or an active ruleset
# for the default branch turns on "Require a pull request before merging",
# "Require review from Code Owners", and "Dismiss stale pull request
# approvals when new commits are pushed".
#
# GitHub reads only the first of .github/CODEOWNERS, CODEOWNERS and
# docs/CODEOWNERS that exists. A project that keeps its rules in one of the
# others should add these two lines there and delete this file.

